# gate-registry.data - Declarative registry for verify-deploy.sh's migrated gates.
#
# Format: one row per gate, TAB-separated, 9 fields:
#   id  name  invoke  dependencies  requires_source_store  timeout_s  cost_class  serialized
#   input_corpus
#
#   id                     Integer gate id, matching verify-deploy.sh's CURRENT_GATE="gateN" and
#                          --only-gate selection numbering. Must be unique; the full migrated
#                          range must be contiguous starting at 1 (checked by lint-gate-registry.sh).
#   name                   Human-readable gate description (NOT currently emitted generically --
#                          each gate's own `say "N. ..."` line is still inside its function body,
#                          preserved verbatim for byte-identical output; this field is informational
#                          metadata for a reader/lint/future consumer, not yet interpolated by the
#                          runner itself).
#   invoke                 The bash function implementing this gate's full check, e.g. `gate1_run`.
#                          Each such function is self-contained: it re-checks `gate_selected`
#                          internally and performs any source-store guard, selection, pass/fail/
#                          FINDINGS_LIST population itself, exactly as the pre-registry inline code
#                          did. The registry's own executor (gate_registry_execute in
#                          lib/gate-registry-lib.sh) does nothing more than look up and call this
#                          function -- see that file's header for why a generic guard/output fold
#                          was judged unsafe for this migrated tranche.
#   dependencies            Comma-separated gate ids this gate depends on, or `-` for none (the
#                          placeholder, NOT a truly empty field -- `IFS=$'\t' read` classifies
#                          tab as IFS-whitespace even as IFS's sole member, so a genuinely empty
#                          field between two tabs silently collapses the delimiter and shifts
#                          every later column by one; gate_registry_load normalizes `-` back to
#                          empty when populating its arrays). `-` for every gate in this registry
#                          today because gates 1-8 (like the research found for the full 23-gate
#                          set) are mutually independent, read-only checks with no producer/
#                          consumer relationship among them. NOW CONSUMED by Phase 7's
#                          gate_registry_exec_concurrent_batch (lib/gate-registry-lib.sh): an
#                          id's WAVE is 1 + max(wave of its own dependencies), enforced via a
#                          hard wait-barrier between waves so a dependent id never starts before
#                          its prerequisite completes. A future gate declaring a real dependency
#                          needs only this field populated -- the scheduler already honours it.
#   requires_source_store   true/false. ACCURATE METADATA for which gates skip (in some form) when
#                          $TARGET is not the source store -- true for gates 3, 5, 6, 7, 8; false
#                          for 1, 2, 4. NOT YET CONSUMED to generically short-circuit a function
#                          call (each function still performs its own check internally, since the
#                          five guarded gates' SKIP message shapes and check ORDER are not uniform
#                          enough to fold losslessly -- gate 5's two-line message and gate 8's
#                          SKIP_SLOW-before-source-store check order are the two concrete
#                          counterexamples; see the plan's Phase 4 for the full reasoning). Future
#                          phases MAY fold this once a richer per-gate message/order field exists,
#                          or may simply leave it as declarative-only metadata permanently.
#   timeout_s               Declared per-gate timeout in seconds, derived from a mechanically
#                          regenerated idle cost model's clean avg_ms (roughly 3x headroom over
#                          the measured average, floor 30s). ENFORCED: verify-deploy.sh's gate
#                          loop calls gate_registry_exec_bounded (lib/gate-registry-lib.sh) with
#                          this value, which runs the gate's invoke function under a real,
#                          killable bound and reports a named, attributable TIMEOUT finding
#                          (gate id + invoke name + bound) rather than hanging the whole battery
#                          indefinitely. Still also validated for presence/well-formedness by
#                          lint-gate-registry.sh.
#   cost_class              One of free/moderate/slow, copied directly from gate-cost-model.csv's
#                          own classification (see measure-gate-costs.sh's header for the class
#                          boundaries). Used by Phase 5's generalized selection surface (selection
#                          by cost class) once that lands; informational only today.
#   serialized              true/false. Declared per gate8's own LOAD_SENSITIVE_BASENAMES-style
#                          parallelism-safety concern (gate8 wraps the full suite battery, which
#                          itself already serializes its own load-sensitive suites internally --
#                          see run-all.sh's own documented set). true only for gate8; false for the
#                          rest, matching the research's own "most gates are independent, read-only
#                          corpus lints" finding. NOW CONSUMED by Phase 7's
#                          gate_registry_exec_concurrent_batch: every serialized=true id runs
#                          alone, ascending id order, strictly before its wave's own pool starts
#                          -- the same LOAD_SENSITIVE_BASENAMES-style "always first, regardless
#                          of the pool's own schedule" posture, ported rather than reinvented.
#                          See context/standards/shell-script-testing.md's "Gate-level
#                          parallelism-safety audit (Phase 7)" section for the full audit that
#                          confirmed no OTHER gate needs this flag (no fixed-path write, lock, or
#                          socket outside its own mktemp-scoped fixture was found in any of the
#                          23 migrated gates' bodies).
#
#   input_corpus           Declarative statement of the DATA this gate's invoke function reads --
#                          NOT the gate's own script/library/function implementation (that is
#                          covered separately by the composite cache key's other four components:
#                          invoke function body, invoked script, sourced libraries, and this
#                          registry row itself -- see scripts/lib/gate-cache-lib.sh). The
#                          placeholder `-` means "corpus not declared, never skippable" -- NOT
#                          "no inputs" -- so a gate with `-` always runs under
#                          `--skip-unchanged`; a genuinely empty field (neither `-` nor a parseable
#                          list) is a lint error, never a silent empty corpus. DECLARATIVE ONLY as
#                          of this field's introduction: it is loaded and queryable but nothing
#                          resolves or consumes it yet (that is the content-addressed digest
#                          library and the --skip-unchanged consult, both later phases).
#
#                          GRAMMAR: a comma-separated list of entries (or the bare placeholder
#                          `-`). Each entry is one of:
#                            @extensions   Named view: the shared `git ls-files` enumeration of
#                                          the `agent-system/extensions` subtree that
#                                          gate_registry_shared_corpus_build already produces for
#                                          Phase 9's shared-corpus lints -- reused here as the
#                                          same NUL-delimited, repo-relative-path producer, never
#                                          re-walked independently.
#                            @repo         Named view: a `git ls-files` enumeration of the WHOLE
#                                          repository, repo-relative. Wider than @extensions;
#                                          reserved for the few gates (e.g. the task-reference and
#                                          shellcheck lints) whose own scan root is the repo, not
#                                          the extensions subtree.
#                            a bare directory path (e.g. `.claude`, `specs`)
#                                          Expands to every tracked path under it (prefix match),
#                                          recursively.
#                            a literal file path (e.g. `specs/state.json`)
#                                          That exact path only.
#                            a glob (e.g. `**/*.sh`, `agent-system/extensions/*/skills/*/SKILL.md`)
#                                          Shell-style glob, matched repo-relative.
#                            !entry        A leading `!` EXCLUDES every path the rest of that
#                                          entry would otherwise match from the corpus built by
#                                          the other entries in the same row (e.g. `@repo,!specs/**`
#                                          is "the whole repo, minus specs/**"). Exclusions apply
#                                          after every non-excluding entry in the row has been
#                                          resolved and unioned, never before.
#                          Resolution order (for the later phase that implements it): expand every
#                          non-`!` entry and union the results; then apply every `!`-prefixed
#                          entry as a subtraction from that union. An entry this lint cannot
#                          classify into one of the shapes above is a lint error, never a
#                          silently-empty corpus.
# This file is edited directly (it is genuinely data, unlike gate-cost-model.csv or
# suite-cost-hints.txt, which are mechanically regenerated) -- adding a migrated gate is a new row
# here plus a `gateN_run` function definition, not a 40-line copy-pasted if/fi block.
1	Event-store and error-store files	gate1_run	-	false	30	free	false	.claude/scripts/events-append.sh,.claude/scripts/events-query.sh,.claude/hooks/events-log-artifact.sh,.claude/hooks/events-log-lifecycle.sh,.claude/context/schemas/events-schema.json,.claude/context/formats/events-format.md,.claude/scripts/errors-append.sh,.claude/context/schemas/errors-schema.json,.claude/context/formats/errors-format.md
2	Hook registrations in the deployed settings.json	gate2_run	-	false	30	free	false	.claude/settings.json
